+## Web push notifications
+
+To enable opt-in push notifications in web browsers, set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and
+`VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to a matching Web Push VAPID key pair in the app and any
+separate job workers. Push requires HTTPS (except on localhost) and outbound
+HTTPS access to the browser push services. People can turn on push for each
+device in **Notification Settings**. On iOS, install Fizzy on the Home Screen
+first.
+
+Keep the private key secret and keep using the same key pair across deployments.
+If you change the key pair, users will need to reset notification permissions
+for Fizzy in the browser and enroll again. Subscriptions are tied to the
+original origin and browser session, so they are not imported between instances.
+
 ## Example
 
 Here's an example of a `docker-compose.yml` that you could use to run Fizzy via `docker compose up`
